s, 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids January to February and August to September each came in under 90% of normal in 32 of them. On that same middle, July to August 2025 landed at 47% of normal and August to September 2025 at 57%. Published so far for 2026, the middle shows January to February at 56% and March to April at 149%. Grid 25096 had its driest year in 1991 at 66%.</p>"}
